<!-- STRUCTURE GUIDE - QUESTIONS -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Code Reading Questions</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p class="section-intro">Open the engine files and answer these questions. Discuss with a partner!</p>
    
    <!-- Part 1 -->
    <details class="skeleton-block" open>
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">1</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Understanding rooms.json</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <p>Open <code>engine/content/rooms.json</code></p>
                <ol>
                    <li>How many rooms are defined?</li>
                    <li>What fields does each room have?</li>
                    <li>How are exits represented?</li>
                    <li>What is the difference between first-visit and revisit descriptions?</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- Part 2 -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Understanding the World Loader</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <p>Open <code>engine/world_loader.py</code></p>
                <ol>
                    <li>What function loads the rooms from JSON?</li>
                    <li>How does the engine look up a room by ID?</li>
                    <li>What happens if a room ID is not found?</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- Part 3 -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">3</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Understanding the Command Parser</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <p>Open <code>engine/command_parser.py</code></p>
                <ol>
                    <li>How does the parser interpret "go north"?</li>
                    <li>What synonyms are supported?</li>
                    <li>How is the parsed command routed to a handler?</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- Part 4 -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">4</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Tracing Your Code</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <p>Think about integration:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>When you call <code>player.get_status()</code>, where does it go?</li>
                    <li>How does the engine use <code>player.inventory.list_items()</code>?</li>
                    <li>What would happen if your Inventory class didn't have <code>has_item()</code>?</li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

